body:
![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The Sieve rule for categorizing "Updates" includes a check for the `List-Unsubscribe` header. This header is a strong indicator of bulk mail (like newsletters), which the document's own definitions classify as "Promotions". This can lead to miscategorizing promotional emails as updates.

To make the rule more precise and align with the defined categories, I suggest removing the `List-Unsubscribe` check from this rule. This will allow the subsequent "Promotions" rule to correctly handle such emails.

```suggestion
if anyof (
    header :contains "X-Mailer" ["GitHub", "GitLab", "Jira"],
    header :contains "from" ["noreply@", "notifications@", "alerts@"]
) {
    if not header :contains "subject" [
        "sale", "offer", "discount", "deal", "promo"
    ] {
        fileinto "Updates";
        stop;
    }
}
```

