![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The code splits the `code` by `#`, assuming the authorization code and state are separated by it. However, the presence of `#` in the code might not always be guaranteed, and relying on it without proper validation can lead to unexpected behavior or errors. It would be more robust to use URLSearchParams to extract the code and state parameters from the callback URL.

```javascript
callback: async (code) => {
  try {
    const urlParams = new URLSearchParams(code);
    const authCode = urlParams.get("code");
    const state = urlParams.get("state");

    if (!authCode || !state) {
      console.error("Missing code or state in callback URL");
      return { type: "failed" };
    }

    const result = await fetch(TOKEN_ENDPOINT, {
      method: "POST",
      headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
      body: JSON.stringify({
        code: authCode,
        state: state,
        grant_type: "authorization_code",
        client_id: CLIENT_ID,
        redirect_uri: REDIRECT_URI,
        code_verifier: pkce.verifier,
      }),
    });
```

