This large `models` object has a lot of duplication across the different model definitions (e.g., `cost`, `limit.context`, `attachment`, `temperature`). To improve maintainability, consider refactoring this to use one or more base objects for common properties, and then use object spreading to create the specific model configurations. This will make future updates to common attributes much easier.

Example:
```javascript
const baseClaudeModel = {
  attachment: true,
  temperature: true,
  cost: { input: 0, output: 0, cache_read: 0, cache_write: 0 },
  limit: { context: 200000 },
  modalities: {
    output: ["text"],
  },
};

const models = {
  "claude-sonnet-4-20250514": {
    ...baseClaudeModel,
    name: "Claude Sonnet 4",
    reasoning: true,
    tool_call: true,
    interleaved: true,
    modalities: { ...baseClaudeModel.modalities, input: ["text", "image", "pdf"] },
    limit: { ...baseClaudeModel.limit, output: 16000 },
    family: "claude-4",
  },
  // ... and so on for other models
};
```

