For better debuggability, consider logging the response body when a request fails. This can provide more context than just the HTTP status, especially if the API returns a specific error message. You'll need to `clone()` the response to read its body here without preventing the caller from also reading it.

```suggestion
  if (!response.ok) {
    const detail = response.status === 429
      ? "rate limited by Anthropic — wait a few minutes before trying again"
      : `HTTP ${response.status}`;
    const body = await response.clone().text().catch(() => '');
    console.error(`[aidevops] OAuth pool: ${context} failed: ${detail}${body ? `. Body: ${body}` : ''}`);
  }
```

